  "body": "User Story: As an officer, I want to be able to see who is present for a specific event because I want to be able to see who is present for point tracking.\r\n\r\nAcceptance Criteria:\r\nOfficers can see who is present at a specific event\r\n- Sunny: An officer opens an event and sees the members marked present, with name and check-in time.\r\n- Rainy: No one has checked in yet, or the attendance data fails to load. The officer sees a clear \"no attendees yet\" or \"try again\" message instead of a blank or broken page.\r\n\r\nThe attendance list is accurate and current\r\n- Sunny: A member logs in, scans the event QR code, and appears on the list (after a refresh at most).\r\n- Rainy: A member scans the QR code twice, or someone who isn't logged in scans it. The member appears only once, and the logged-out person is asked to log in and is not marked present until they do.\r\n\r\nImplements officer attendance viewing and member QR check-in for the two assigned Jira stories. Officers can configure event coordinates, distance limits, and point values, display a QR code, and view attendee names and check-in times. Members sign in, submit their location, and receive attendance confirmation with a single point award.\r\n\r\n- Rejects duplicate scans and distant or invalid locations; uses a transaction, member lock, and unique index to protect attendance and points.\r\n- Includes empty/loading-error states, preserves the check-in destination after Google login, and filters coordinates from request logs.\r\n- Adds database migrations; run `bundle install` and `bundle exec rails db:migrate` after checkout.\r\n\r\nValidation on the feature branch: 85 RSpec examples, 0 failures, 1 existing pending example; 8 JavaScript tests passed; RuboCop passed. Tests cover concurrent scans, login return, role restrictions, save failures, and point awards. New teammate changes on main were fetched after this validation and are not yet integrated into the feature branch.\r\n\r\nStill to verify before marking the stories Done: a real phone QR/location walkthrough on a reachable HTTPS deployment. Localhost is only suitable for testing on the same computer. Location is browser-reported and is not spoof-proof proof of physical presence.\r\n\r\nDefinition of Done -\r\nA story is done when its acceptance criteria are met and every item in the team PR template is satisfied: \r\n(A) code review by a non-author, coding standard met, RuboCop checked with output/CI link, and setup changes documented; \r\n(B) the human-only maintainability checks (meaningful comments and names, skinny controllers, thin views, DRY, Rails conventions, foreign keys, enums, nested routes); \r\n(C) tests added or updated and passing. Any deferred items or RuboCop exclusions are explained in Section D of the PR.",
